WEBVTT

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.610
It has been nearly half a year now
since life with my Cub first began.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.030
The school excursion was over
and I was living my usual day-to-day life.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:41.870
My brief adventure in riding to
Kamakura after missing the bus...

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.460
...now seems like it was a dream.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.470
How is your Hunter Cub riding?

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:28.890
It's only been a thousand kilometers,
so I'm still breaking it in.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.730
But never mind me, it's getting cold.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:42.700
I feel like charging anyone
who says it's cold today a fee.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:46.540
When it's cold, it's cold.
What do you expect us to do?

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.790
Okay, pay up. Next time,
I pull your license.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:53.380
I don't have any savings left
after buying my Hunter Cub.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:59.380
Okay, I'll settle for this, instead.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.510
When did that get there?

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:06.270
The seasons are changing,
and the wind is growing chillier.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.810
However, for some reason,

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:12.860
the atmosphere in the school
had taken on an unusual fervor.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.610
Good morning.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:17.030
Good morning.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.190
What's in there?

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:20.320
Some scraps that were in
the Home Economics room.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.780
They said if we could use any of it,
we were welcome to it.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:27.620
The low-grade excitement in the air
and the chill in the wind...

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.370
Autumn had arrived.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:07.010
"2nd Year"

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.470
This might be nice.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.140
Where would we use it?

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:17.440
Hmm... Oh, Reiko-<i>chan</i>, good morning.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.690
Good morning.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.320
Did you stop by this morning?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.440
I sure did. You sure left early, huh?

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.990
Mm-hmm. There's so much to get ready
for the culture festival, after all.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:29.950
"Stop by"?

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:32.450
Her family runs the bakery
I always buy from.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:33.870
Ah...

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.380
The culture festival, huh?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.970
Apparently, our class is putting on a bar.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:46.220
What's a bar?

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:47.970
An Italian-style café.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:49.340
They're serving coffee?

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:53.140
Espresso. Daiichi High
had their culture festival

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:57.310
and they're apparently lending us
the espresso machine, the flatware,

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:00.270
and whatever else they used
for next to nothing.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.940
Hmm...

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.320
What do you think about this?

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.070
--It's nice.
--Aw...

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:09.030
I guess work gloves aren't
going to cut it anymore.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:11.990
If you need to change them
for something else, you should.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.830
It's going to get colder pretty soon.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:19.790
Some streets will freeze over
and become impassable.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.590
We need to do something
before that happens.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:41.980
We're done!

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.820
What are you doing today?

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:51.320
Um, excuse me, please!

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.410
We're from the culture festival
executive committee.

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:59.790
So, um, we would like to decorate
the room for our culture festival bar.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:02.880
We're going to need volunteers
to help decorate,

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:07.340
so anyone who has time right now,
could you please stay and help us?

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:08.630
Hey, what do you think?

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.090
--Why not?
--Sure.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:11.840
I'm in, I'm in!

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.890
How about it?

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:18.270
Thank you. There are materials
and things all ready to go.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.310
Right now, this comes first.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.810
Oh...

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.820
Is this bar going to serve coffee?

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:28.150
More like espressos and cappuccinos.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.150
I can't wait to see it.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.870
Where are we going?

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.200
The secondhand shops in Kofu.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:43.330
I need to start thinking about getting
my Cub ready for winter, too.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:10.610
Ah. Let's go check out over there.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:12.150
Huh? What gives?

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:14.240
We aren't here for that today.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.470
--Here.
--Thanks.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.480
There really is nothing that beats
non-slip work gloves.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:29.150
Are they really that good?

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.230
You know what?

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:32.900
In a number of what we refer to
as developed nations,

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:37.870
fighter pilots and transport pilots
still use non-slip work gloves.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:41.870
Which goes to show that of all the gloves
all over the world, work gloves--

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:42.790
Sure, sure.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.040
Ah! Hey, listen to me! Come on, really.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:47.920
Sure, sure.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.710
Koguma-<i>san</i>!

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.010
Koguma-<i>san</i>?

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.600
Okay, ready to go?

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.390
Huh?!

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:05.890
Hey, are you serious?

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:07.730
The teacher can't drive us?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:10.110
She said she had another important
errand to attend to, so no.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.190
Nat-<i>chan</i>, didn't you ask
the teacher before?

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:15.320
Huh? I thought <i>you </i>were asking her.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:16.990
Don't look at me!

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:19.820
Forget about that, if we don't
get all that stuff over here today,

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.660
we won't have things ready
in time for tomorrow!

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:26.660
Sounds like trouble. That's too bad.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.170
Let's go.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.840
Mm-hmm...

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.760
Can we get someone's parents
to drive their car?

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.220
Or the train? Or, yeah, motorbikes?

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:40.550
It's an espresso machine
and other fragile stuff!

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:44.390
How dumb are you? You can't
carry that stuff on a motorbike!

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:46.430
Then what are we supposed to do?!

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:49.850
That's what we're trying
to figure out right now!

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:55.690
Uh, everyone, stay calm.
Let's just stay calm.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:58.530
You still have that rig, right?

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.120
One of the dampers is shot.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:11.380
We might be able to help you out.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:15.380
U-Um, "might" how?

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.050
Is this everything that you
need moved here today?

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.380
"Tablecloths x 10" "Trays x 5"
"Showcase" "Espresso Machine"

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.380
Oh, mm-hmm.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:25.260
There's something I need to go borrow,
so I'm off to the faculty room.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.480
They have a really good one in the gym.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.030
This will be a piece of cake for our Cubs.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:18.690
Nice work.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.030
I see you managed to borrow a trailer.

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:28.790
The tire pressure and axle
bearings both check out.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.580
The handle mount doesn't have
any problems with it, either.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.210
I think this is going to
work over here, too.

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:37.210
Who'd have guessed the day would
ever come when that would be useful?

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.710
Huh? This delivery rig is widely
regarded as a masterpiece,

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:43.340
even among all the other
Cub equipment out there.

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:47.510
With this thing, even an amateur driver
can keep their soba from spilling

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:49.470
and their <i>donburi </i>bowls from breaking!

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:53.140
That's why we need it. Let's get started.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:18.000
Say, are you sure that lame
trailer has to hitch up

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.000
to the world's coolest Hunter Cub?

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.670
My Cub is only 52 cc.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.590
Yours is 110 cc, and has
more power and torque.

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:28.390
That is true...

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.830
There.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.380
Not bad, huh?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.680
Reiko...

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:09.930
Mm-hmm.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.980
They both look all right to me.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.450
E-Excuse me...

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:35.000
Did you bring them?

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.660
They're inside.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:46.720
Huh? Percolators?

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:49.890
Be sure to learn how to
use them before you leave.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:52.220
If this trip doesn't end up successfully,

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.180
you can use those to put on
an early American saloon.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:59.560
There's a Winchester rifle, some cowboy
clothes, a Republic of Texas flag,

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:03.690
and the swinging doors that every saloon
must have in the drama club room.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:09.320
Super Ono sells canned pork and beans,
and ready-made apple pie, too.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:14.700
Whenever you take any action,
always have a backup plan, just in case.

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.470
Okay, we're off.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:37.330
"Kofu Daiichi Prefectural High School"

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:40.830
Wait right here.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:42.250
Okay.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.580
Right, thanks for coming.

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:45.710
"Faculty Room"

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:47.420
"Faculty Room"
Excuse me.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:53.970
Ah! Long time no see!

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:01.680
You seem to be doing well.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.980
I'm here to borrow what we
need for our culture festival.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:09.610
Oh? We were told that your teacher
was coming by to pick it up in her car.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:12.690
Hmm?

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:25.500
Ah, now I get it.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:30.670
It's all ready to go.
I'll bring it right out, okay?

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:31.960
Okay.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:43.810
That's everything.

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:47.770
I have to admit, these Cubs
of yours are amazing.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:51.150
My granddad has one.
Maybe I'll ask him if I can have it.

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:53.360
You should buy one new.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:56.070
The rumors that Cubs are
indestructible aren't true, after all.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:18:00.780
Riding old Cubs can be asking for trouble.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.290
I wouldn't mind that kind of trouble.

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:16.680
Okay, thanks.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:18.890
Thank you very much.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.220
Be careful!

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:47.500
"Mukawa High School Culture Festival"

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.000
"Haunted Mansion"

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:58.680
My name is Umahachi! In grief
for the late Omasa, Sukesada--

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:07.730
"Welcome to the Italian bar"

00:19:04.520 --> 00:19:07.730
Welcome! Table for two, please!

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:08.810
--Welcome!
--Welcome!

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:12.190
Welcome. Right this way, please.

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:17.860
Thank you for waiting.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:21.700
Espresso and lettuce-and-ham
panini, order up.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.870
Coming.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:25.290
Here, thanks.

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.750
You bet.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:40.800
The teacher said to figure out the cost of
our gas and submit it for reimbursement.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:44.720
Ugh, everyone seems to think
that gasoline is all it takes

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.470
to keep cars and bikes running.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:49.940
About a hundred yen, round trip?

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:51.600
I'll pretend I was going to buy a coffee,

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:55.190
but dropped my money and it rolled
under the vending machine instead.

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.900
What are you doing after this?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:59.820
Hmm... I'd like to stretch my legs...

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:02.530
W-Wait! Please wait!

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:11.170
I'm sorry I haven't been able
to thank you properly.

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:14.290
Here is a token of our feelings.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.420
It's coffee...

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:38.150
Everyone is grateful to you two.
Really. But we're all so busy, so...

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.490
This will do.

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.450
Your motorbikes sure are terrific.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.620
I've never thought of them as terrific.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:49.540
It's Cubs that are terrific, Shii-<i>chan</i>.

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:58.840
I'd like to ride one, too.

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:03.590
But I could never handle a motorbike.
I fall off my bicycle too much as it is.

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:06.800
You shouldn't do anything that
you think you can't handle.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:08.180
Huh?

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.350
If you ride a Cub while you're spooked,

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:15.650
the Cub will be spooked right back
at you and fling you off of its seat.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:22.650
They're made so that you have to want
to ride them, or they won't let you.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:28.910
We'll bring these back up
to the classroom later,

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:32.120
so, Shii-<i>chan</i>, you should hurry
on back to your counter.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:37.210
Oh, then... thanks again so much, really.

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:55.560
Awfully sweet, huh?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:02.230
I'll take these back. You check
out some cold-weather gloves.

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:03.820
Roger that!

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:09.780
Two cappuccinos!

00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:10.700
Okay.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:13.330
One latte macchiato, please.

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:19.130
I found myself unexpectedly pulled into
the middle of the culture festival.

00:22:19.130 --> 00:22:22.800
This delicate young lady,
who was so busy taking care of matters,

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:25.630
now looms a little larger
than she did before.

00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:33.560
A pale, washed-out light blue--
that was my impression of her.

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:38.020
But it appears now that I was mistaken.

00:22:38.020 --> 00:22:40.940
Yes, for you see...

00:22:40.940 --> 00:22:44.780
...though the hue was a light one,
it was the color of a bright and sunny...

00:22:46.110 --> 00:22:46.610
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 7"
"The Girl of Summer-Sky Aqua"

00:22:46.610 --> 00:22:48.660
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 7"
"The Girl of Summer-Sky Aqua"
...summer sky.

00:22:48.660 --> 00:22:51.120
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 7"
"The Girl of Summer-Sky Aqua"

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:22.960
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 8"
"Shii's Place"

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:26.000
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 8"
"Shii's Place"
Episode 8: "Shii's Place."
